Coroutines are lightweight threads managed by the Kotlin runtime. A `suspend` function can pause without blocking its carrier thread, so thousands of coroutines can share a small pool.

Structured concurrency ties every coroutine to a `CoroutineScope`; cancelling the scope cancels its children, which keeps lifecycles predictable.

```kotlin
fun main() = runBlocking {
    val job = launch { delay(100); println("done") }
    job.join()
}
```
